{
  "$comment": "Cooking methods offered as alternatives to the one a recipe authored, so a reader can ask \"what if this were boiled instead of fried\" and get an answer rather than a paragraph. PRD §6.1 makes the recipe editable because the assumption is the largest source of variance; the method is the second largest after the grams, and until now it was the one assumption the reader could not touch.",
  "basis": "Every operation below is a real row in the USDA retention table, cited and transcribed in data/factors/retention.json. What is authored here is only the grouping: which operations are a sensible choice for the same ingredient. That grouping follows the food groups the USDA table itself uses in its descriptions — EGGS, CHICKEN, VEG,GREENS and so on — and no operation appears in more than one group. It is a judgement about which questions are worth asking, not a nutritional claim: the numbers all come from USDA.",
  "catatan": "Memilih cara masak yang berbeda dari yang ditulis resep membuat faktor yield resep itu tidak berlaku lagi, jadi berat matangnya jadi tidak diketahui dan disebut sebagai kekosongan. Itu jujur: faktor yield-nya untuk cara masak yang tadi, bukan yang baru.",
